{"reference":"Exodus 1","book":"Exodus","chapter":1,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"cultural_context","title":"Coerced labor","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Exodus describes coerced brick labor in which supervisors stop supplying straw while demanding the same daily output. Those economic and administrative details make the pressure on the laborers concrete before any wider comparison is introduced.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_exodus_001_effa44e7771ef6788b03c885"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The movement of Exodus","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The book of Exodus moves from oppression and deliverance to covenant, covenant breach and renewal, tabernacle construction, and the arrival of divine glory. The opening oppression belongs to that wider movement rather than standing as the book's endpoint.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_exodus_001_3d24dcb5d4d50cca07233059"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
